IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `aia-core`
IMPORT `aia-timeline`
IMPORT `P4-gate`

-- P4-art-36: Article 36 (Changes to notifications). Not changed by the Omnibus (marker `▼B`): one text, both versions.
-- Every function takes `the date asked` first and answers NOTHING before Chapter III Section 4 applies (2 August 2025).
-- Periods in days are added to a date; periods in months and years use the `add months` and `add years` of daydate (fork F-months).
-- A duty whose "where" or "whenever" is unmet answers NOTHING (fork F-unmet-where); a bare "shall" not done answers JUST FALSE (fork F-bare-shall).

§ `Article 36: the parties and acts of the regulative rules`

DECLARE `Art 36 party` IS ONE OF
    `Art 36 notifying authority`
    `Art 36 notified body`
    `Art 36 provider`
    `Art 36 national competent authority`

DECLARE `Art 36 act` IS ONE OF
    `Art 36(1) notify the Commission and the other Member States of the relevant change via the electronic notification tool`
    `Art 36(3) inform the notifying authority and the providers concerned of the planned cessation`
    `Art 36(3) withdraw the designation of the notified body that has ceased its activity`
    `Art 36(4) investigate the matter with the utmost diligence`
    `Art 36(4) inform the notified body of the objections and give it the possibility to make its views known`
    `Art 36(4) restrict, suspend or withdraw the designation`
    `Art 36(4) inform the Commission and the other Member States of the measure`
    `Art 36(5) inform the providers concerned`
    `Art 36(6) take appropriate steps to ensure that the files of the notified body are kept and made available`
    `Art 36(7)(a) assess the impact on the certificates issued by the notified body`
    `Art 36(7)(b) submit a report on its findings to the Commission and the other Member States`
    `Art 36(7)(c) require the notified body to suspend or withdraw the certificates which were unduly issued`
    `Art 36(7)(d) inform the Commission and the Member States about the certificates the suspension or withdrawal of which it has required`
    `Art 36(7)(e) provide the national competent authorities with all relevant information about the certificates`
    `Art 36(8)(b) confirm in writing that another qualified notified body is temporarily assuming the functions`
    `Art 36(9) inform the Commission, the other Member States and the other notified bodies of the change of designation`

DECLARE `Art 36(2) procedures` IS ONE OF
    `Art 36(2) the procedures of Articles 29 and 30`
    `Art 36(2) the procedures of paragraphs (3) to (9) of Article 36`

§ `Article 36(1): notifying relevant changes`

-- src:601 | 1. The notifying authority shall notify the Commission and the other Member States of any relevant changes to the notification of a notified body via the electronic notification tool referred to in Article 30(2).
@ref Art 36(1) (src:601)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `there is a relevant change to the notification of a notified body` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notifying authority has notified the Commission and the other Member States of the change` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notifying authority used the electronic notification tool referred to in Article 30(2)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 36(1) the notifying authority has notified the relevant change` MEANS
    IF NOT (`Art 28 to 39 the notified bodies group applies on the date asked` `the date asked`)
    THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Chapter III Section 4 applies from 2 August 2025
    ELSE IF NOT `there is a relevant change to the notification of a notified body`
         THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "of any relevant changes to the notification" (fork F-unmet-where)
         ELSE JUST (   `the notifying authority has notified the Commission and the other Member States of the change`
                   AND `the notifying authority used the electronic notification tool referred to in Article 30(2)`)  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall notify the Commission and the other Member States of any relevant changes ... via the electronic notification tool" (a bare "shall" not done)

-- No time limit and no consequence is stated, so no trace can show this rule breached.
-- src:601 | 1. The notifying authority shall notify the Commission and the other Member States of any relevant changes to the notification of a notified body via the electronic notification tool referred to in Article 30(2).
@ref Art 36(1) (src:601)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Art 36 party` `Art 36 act`
`Art 36(1) the duty of the notifying authority to notify the relevant change` MEANS
    IF NOT (`Art 28 to 39 the notified bodies group applies on the date asked` `the date asked`)
    THEN FULFILLED  -- nothing is owed before Chapter III Section 4 applies
    ELSE PARTY `Art 36 notifying authority`
         MUST `Art 36(1) notify the Commission and the other Member States of the relevant change via the electronic notification tool`
         HENCE FULFILLED

§ `Article 36(2): which procedures apply to a change`

-- src:602 | 2. The procedures laid down in Articles 29 and 30 shall apply to extensions of the scope of the notification.
-- src:603 | For changes to the notification other than extensions of its scope, the procedures laid down in paragraphs (3) to (9) shall apply.
@ref Art 36(2) (src:602-603)
-- Gloss: widening the scope of a notification goes through Articles 29 and 30 again; any other change goes through paragraphs 3 to 9 of this Article. (The second subparagraph says "paragraphs (3) to (9)" without naming the Article: read as the paragraphs of Article 36, fork F-36-2.)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the change is an extension of the scope of the notification` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the change is a change to the notification other than an extension of its scope` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE `Art 36(2) procedures`
`Art 36(2) the procedures that apply to the change to the notification` MEANS
    IF NOT (`Art 28 to 39 the notified bodies group applies on the date asked` `the date asked`)
    THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Chapter III Section 4 applies from 2 August 2025
    ELSE IF `the change is an extension of the scope of the notification`
         THEN JUST `Art 36(2) the procedures of Articles 29 and 30`  -- "The procedures laid down in Articles 29 and 30 shall apply to extensions of the scope of the notification"
         ELSE IF `the change is a change to the notification other than an extension of its scope`
              THEN JUST `Art 36(2) the procedures of paragraphs (3) to (9) of Article 36`  -- "For changes to the notification other than extensions of its scope, the procedures laid down in paragraphs (3) to (9) shall apply"
              ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the paragraph speaks of changes to the notification

§ `Article 36(3): ceasing activities`

-- src:604 | 3. Where a notified body decides to cease its conformity assessment activities, it shall inform the notifying authority and the providers concerned as soon as possible and, in the case of a planned cessation, at least one year before ceasing its activities. The certificates of the notified body may remain valid for a period of nine months after cessation of the notified body’s activities, on condition that another notified body has confirmed in writing that it will assume responsibilities for the high-risk AI systems covered by those certificates. The latter notified body shall complete a full assessment of the high-risk AI systems affected by the end of that nine-month-period before issuing new certificates for those systems. Where the notified body has ceased its activity, the notifying authority shall withdraw the designation.
@ref Art 36(3) (src:604)
-- Gloss: a body that decides to stop tells the notifying authority and the providers concerned as soon as possible, and at least one year ahead if the stop is planned. For a stop that is not planned the text gives no period ("as soon as possible"), so a body that has informed both is NOTHING, not TRUE.
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the notified body has decided to cease its conformity assessment activities` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the cessation is a planned cessation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notified body has informed the notifying authority and the providers concerned` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date on which the notified body informed the notifying authority and the providers concerned` IS A DATE
      `the date on which the notified body ceases its activities` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 36(3) first sentence the notified body has informed the notifying authority and the providers of its cessation` MEANS
    IF NOT (`Art 28 to 39 the notified bodies group applies on the date asked` `the date asked`)
    THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Chapter III Section 4 applies from 2 August 2025
    ELSE IF NOT `the notified body has decided to cease its conformity assessment activities`
         THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Where a notified body decides to cease its conformity assessment activities" (fork F-unmet-where)
         ELSE IF NOT `the notified body has informed the notifying authority and the providers concerned`
              THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "it shall inform the notifying authority and the providers concerned" (a bare "shall" not done)
              ELSE IF `the cessation is a planned cessation`
                   THEN JUST (`the date on which the notified body informed the notifying authority and the providers concerned` AT MOST (`add years` `the date on which the notified body ceases its activities` (0 MINUS 1)))  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "in the case of a planned cessation, at least one year before ceasing its activities"
                   ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (undefined term): "as soon as possible" gives no period

-- The deadline for a planned cessation as a regulative rule: the clock starts on the day the body decides; the deadline is one year before it ceases.
-- src:604 | 3. Where a notified body decides to cease its conformity assessment activities, it shall inform the notifying authority and the providers concerned as soon as possible and, in the case of a planned cessation, at least one year before ceasing its activities. The certificates of the notified body may remain valid for a period of nine months after cessation of the notified body’s activities, on condition that another notified body has confirmed in writing that it will assume responsibilities for the high-risk AI systems covered by those certificates. The latter notified body shall complete a full assessment of the high-risk AI systems affected by the end of that nine-month-period before issuing new certificates for those systems. Where the notified body has ceased its activity, the notifying authority shall withdraw the designation.
@ref Art 36(3) (src:604)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the date on which the notified body decides to cease` IS A DATE
      `the date on which the notified body ceases its activities` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Art 36 party` `Art 36 act`
`Art 36(3) the duty of the notified body to inform the notifying authority and the providers of a planned cessation` MEANS
    IF NOT (`Art 28 to 39 the notified bodies group applies on the date asked` `the date asked`)
    THEN FULFILLED  -- nothing is owed before Chapter III Section 4 applies
    ELSE PARTY `Art 36 notified body`
         MUST `Art 36(3) inform the notifying authority and the providers concerned of the planned cessation`
         WITHIN (Day (`add years` `the date on which the notified body ceases its activities` (0 MINUS 1))) MINUS (Day `the date on which the notified body decides to cease`)
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST BREACH BY `Art 36 notified body` BECAUSE "the notifying authority and the providers concerned were not informed at least one year before the planned cessation"

-- src:604 | 3. Where a notified body decides to cease its conformity assessment activities, it shall inform the notifying authority and the providers concerned as soon as possible and, in the case of a planned cessation, at least one year before ceasing its activities. The certificates of the notified body may remain valid for a period of nine months after cessation of the notified body’s activities, on condition that another notified body has confirmed in writing that it will assume responsibilities for the high-risk AI systems covered by those certificates. The latter notified body shall complete a full assessment of the high-risk AI systems affected by the end of that nine-month-period before issuing new certificates for those systems. Where the notified body has ceased its activity, the notifying authority shall withdraw the designation.
@ref Art 36(3) (src:604)
-- Gloss: the certificates may stay valid for nine months after the body stops, on condition that another notified body has confirmed in writing that it will take over responsibility for the systems they cover. A "may" on a condition: NOTHING where the condition is not met (fork F-36-3).
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the date on which the notified body ceased its activities` IS A DATE
      `another notified body has confirmed in writing that it will assume responsibilities for the high-risk AI systems covered by those certificates` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 36(3) second sentence the certificates may remain valid after the cessation` MEANS
    IF NOT (`Art 28 to 39 the notified bodies group applies on the date asked` `the date asked`)
    THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Chapter III Section 4 applies from 2 August 2025
    ELSE IF `the date asked` LESS THAN `the date on which the notified body ceased its activities`
         THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the sentence speaks of validity "after cessation of the notified body's activities"
         ELSE IF NOT `another notified body has confirmed in writing that it will assume responsibilities for the high-risk AI systems covered by those certificates`
              THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "on condition that another notified body has confirmed in writing" (a power named by "may")
              ELSE JUST (`the date asked` AT MOST (`add months` `the date on which the notified body ceased its activities` 9))  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "may remain valid for a period of nine months after cessation" (a period the text fixes: outside it, no)

-- src:604 | 3. Where a notified body decides to cease its conformity assessment activities, it shall inform the notifying authority and the providers concerned as soon as possible and, in the case of a planned cessation, at least one year before ceasing its activities. The certificates of the notified body may remain valid for a period of nine months after cessation of the notified body’s activities, on condition that another notified body has confirmed in writing that it will assume responsibilities for the high-risk AI systems covered by those certificates. The latter notified body shall complete a full assessment of the high-risk AI systems affected by the end of that nine-month-period before issuing new certificates for those systems. Where the notified body has ceased its activity, the notifying authority shall withdraw the designation.
@ref Art 36(3) (src:604)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the date on which the former notified body ceased its activities` IS A DATE
      `the date on which the latter notified body completed a full assessment of the high-risk AI systems affected` IS A DATE
      `the latter notified body has issued new certificates for those systems` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date on which the latter notified body first issued new certificates` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 36(3) third sentence the latter notified body has completed the full assessment before issuing new certificates` MEANS
    `Art 28 to 39 the answer when the group applies` `the date asked`
        (   `the date on which the latter notified body completed a full assessment of the high-risk AI systems affected` AT MOST (`add months` `the date on which the former notified body ceased its activities` 9)
        AND (   (NOT `the latter notified body has issued new certificates for those systems`)
             OR `the date on which the latter notified body completed a full assessment of the high-risk AI systems affected` AT MOST `the date on which the latter notified body first issued new certificates`))
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The latter notified body shall complete a full assessment of the high-risk AI systems affected by the end of that nine-month-period before issuing new certificates for those systems" (a bare "shall" not done; "before issuing" read as on or before the day of the first issue, fork F-36-3)

-- src:604 | 3. Where a notified body decides to cease its conformity assessment activities, it shall inform the notifying authority and the providers concerned as soon as possible and, in the case of a planned cessation, at least one year before ceasing its activities. The certificates of the notified body may remain valid for a period of nine months after cessation of the notified body’s activities, on condition that another notified body has confirmed in writing that it will assume responsibilities for the high-risk AI systems covered by those certificates. The latter notified body shall complete a full assessment of the high-risk AI systems affected by the end of that nine-month-period before issuing new certificates for those systems. Where the notified body has ceased its activity, the notifying authority shall withdraw the designation.
@ref Art 36(3) (src:604)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the notified body has ceased its activity` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notifying authority has withdrawn the designation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 36(3) fourth sentence the notifying authority has withdrawn the designation of a notified body that has ceased` MEANS
    IF NOT (`Art 28 to 39 the notified bodies group applies on the date asked` `the date asked`)
    THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Chapter III Section 4 applies from 2 August 2025
    ELSE IF NOT `the notified body has ceased its activity`
         THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Where the notified body has ceased its activity" (fork F-unmet-where)
         ELSE JUST `the notifying authority has withdrawn the designation`  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the notifying authority shall withdraw the designation" (a bare "shall" not done)

-- No time limit and no consequence is stated, so no trace can show this rule breached.
