§ `Article 36(4): doubts about a notified body`

-- src:605 | 4. Where a notifying authority has sufficient reason to consider that a notified body no longer meets the requirements laid down in Article 31, or that it is failing to fulfil its obligations, the notifying authority shall without delay investigate the matter with the utmost diligence. In that context, it shall inform the notified body concerned about the objections raised and give it the possibility to make its views known. If the notifying authority comes to the conclusion that the notified body no longer meets the requirements laid down in Article 31 or that it is failing to fulfil its obligations, it shall restrict, suspend or withdraw the designation as appropriate, depending on the seriousness of the failure to meet those requirements or fulfil those obligations. It shall immediately inform the Commission and the other Member States accordingly.
@ref Art 36(4) (src:605)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the notifying authority has sufficient reason to consider that the notified body no longer meets the requirements laid down in Article 31, or that it is failing to fulfil its obligations` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notifying authority has investigated the matter without delay with the utmost diligence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 36(4) first sentence the notifying authority has investigated the matter` MEANS
    IF NOT (`Art 28 to 39 the notified bodies group applies on the date asked`  `the date asked`)
    THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Chapter III Section 4 applies from 2 August 2025
    ELSE IF NOT `the notifying authority has sufficient reason to consider that the notified body no longer meets the requirements laid down in Article 31, or that it is failing to fulfil its obligations`
         THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Where a notifying authority has sufficient reason to consider" (fork F-unmet-where)
         ELSE JUST `the notifying authority has investigated the matter without delay with the utmost diligence`  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the notifying authority shall without delay investigate the matter with the utmost diligence" (a bare "shall" not done; "without delay" gives no number of days)

-- src:605 | 4. Where a notifying authority has sufficient reason to consider that a notified body no longer meets the requirements laid down in Article 31, or that it is failing to fulfil its obligations, the notifying authority shall without delay investigate the matter with the utmost diligence. In that context, it shall inform the notified body concerned about the objections raised and give it the possibility to make its views known. If the notifying authority comes to the conclusion that the notified body no longer meets the requirements laid down in Article 31 or that it is failing to fulfil its obligations, it shall restrict, suspend or withdraw the designation as appropriate, depending on the seriousness of the failure to meet those requirements or fulfil those obligations. It shall immediately inform the Commission and the other Member States accordingly.
@ref Art 36(4) (src:605)
-- Gloss: the notified body is told what is objected to and may state its views before any measure is taken.
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the notifying authority has sufficient reason to consider that the notified body no longer meets the requirements laid down in Article 31, or that it is failing to fulfil its obligations` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notifying authority has informed the notified body concerned about the objections raised` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notifying authority has given the notified body the possibility to make its views known` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
