-- src:605 | 4. Where a notifying authority has sufficient reason to consider that a notified body no longer meets the requirements laid down in Article 31, or that it is failing to fulfil its obligations, the notifying authority shall without delay investigate the matter with the utmost diligence. In that context, it shall inform the notified body concerned about the objections raised and give it the possibility to make its views known. If the notifying authority comes to the conclusion that the notified body no longer meets the requirements laid down in Article 31 or that it is failing to fulfil its obligations, it shall restrict, suspend or withdraw the designation as appropriate, depending on the seriousness of the failure to meet those requirements or fulfil those obligations. It shall immediately inform the Commission and the other Member States accordingly.
@ref Art 36(4) (src:605)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Art 36 party` `Art 36 act`
`Art 36(4) the duty of the notifying authority to inform the Commission and the other Member States` MEANS
    IF NOT (`Art 28 to 39 the notified bodies group applies on the date asked` `the date asked`)
    THEN FULFILLED  -- nothing is owed before Chapter III Section 4 applies
    ELSE PARTY `Art 36 notifying authority`
         MUST `Art 36(4) inform the Commission and the other Member States of the measure`
         HENCE FULFILLED

§ `Article 36(5): telling the providers within 10 days`

-- src:606 | 5. Where its designation has been suspended, restricted, or fully or partially withdrawn, the notified body shall inform the providers concerned within 10 days.
@ref Art 36(5) (src:606)
-- Gloss: when a body's designation is suspended, restricted, or withdrawn in whole or in part, the body tells the providers concerned within 10 days.
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the designation has been suspended, restricted, or fully or partially withdrawn` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date of the suspension, restriction or withdrawal` IS A DATE
      `the notified body has informed the providers concerned` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date on which the notified body informed the providers concerned` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 36(5) the notified body has informed the providers concerned within 10 days` MEANS
    IF NOT (`Art 28 to 39 the notified bodies group applies on the date asked` `the date asked`)
    THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Chapter III Section 4 applies from 2 August 2025
    ELSE IF NOT `the designation has been suspended, restricted, or fully or partially withdrawn`
         THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Where its designation has been suspended, restricted, or fully or partially withdrawn" (fork F-unmet-where)
         ELSE JUST (   `the notified body has informed the providers concerned`
                   AND `the date on which the notified body informed the providers concerned` AT MOST (`the date of the suspension, restriction or withdrawal` PLUS 10))  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the notified body shall inform the providers concerned within 10 days" (a period the text fixes)

-- The deadline as a regulative rule: the clock starts on the day of the suspension, restriction or withdrawal. A missed deadline reaches BREACH.
-- src:606 | 5. Where its designation has been suspended, restricted, or fully or partially withdrawn, the notified body shall inform the providers concerned within 10 days.
@ref Art 36(5) (src:606)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Art 36 party` `Art 36 act`
`Art 36(5) the duty of the notified body to inform the providers concerned within 10 days` MEANS
    IF NOT (`Art 28 to 39 the notified bodies group applies on the date asked` `the date asked`)
    THEN FULFILLED  -- nothing is owed before Chapter III Section 4 applies
    ELSE PARTY `Art 36 notified body`
         MUST `Art 36(5) inform the providers concerned`
         WITHIN 10
