§ `Article 36(8): certificates after a suspension or restriction`

-- The two circumstances of the list. Each is a BOOLEAN: whether the circumstance holds.
-- src:615 | (a) the notifying authority has confirmed, within one month of the suspension or restriction, that there is no risk to health, safety or fundamental rights in relation to certificates affected by the suspension or restriction, and the notifying authority has outlined a timeline for actions to remedy the suspension or restriction; or
@ref Art 36(8)(a) (src:615)
-- Gloss: the authority confirmed, within one month of the suspension or restriction, that there is no risk, and set out a timeline for putting the problem right.
GIVEN `the date of the suspension or restriction` IS A DATE
      `the notifying authority has confirmed that there is no risk to health, safety or fundamental rights in relation to the certificates affected by the suspension or restriction` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date of that confirmation` IS A DATE
      `the notifying authority has outlined a timeline for actions to remedy the suspension or restriction` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 36(8)(a) the circumstance of point (a) holds` MEANS
        `the notifying authority has confirmed that there is no risk to health, safety or fundamental rights in relation to the certificates affected by the suspension or restriction`
    AND `the date of that confirmation` AT MOST (`add months` `the date of the suspension or restriction` 1)
    AND `the notifying authority has outlined a timeline for actions to remedy the suspension or restriction`
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(a) the notifying authority has confirmed, within one month of the suspension or restriction, that there is no risk ... and the notifying authority has outlined a timeline" (a limb of a list the text introduces with "in one of the following circumstances")

-- src:616 | (b) the notifying authority has confirmed that no certificates relevant to the suspension will be issued, amended or re-issued during the course of the suspension or restriction, and states whether the notified body has the capability of continuing to monitor and remain responsible for existing certificates issued for the period of the suspension or restriction; in the event that the notifying authority determines that the notified body does not have the capability to support existing certificates issued, the provider of the system covered by the certificate shall confirm in writing to the national competent authorities of the Member State in which it has its registered place of business, within three months of the suspension or restriction, that another qualified notified body is temporarily assuming the functions of the notified body to monitor and remain responsible for the certificates during the period of suspension or restriction.
@ref Art 36(8)(b) (src:616)
-- Gloss: the authority confirmed that no relevant certificates will be issued, amended or re-issued meanwhile, and says whether the body can keep monitoring the existing ones; if it cannot, the provider confirms in writing within three months that another qualified notified body is stepping in.
GIVEN `the date of the suspension or restriction` IS A DATE
      `the notifying authority has confirmed that no certificates relevant to the suspension will be issued, amended or re-issued during the course of the suspension or restriction` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notifying authority states whether the notified body has the capability of continuing to monitor and remain responsible for existing certificates` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notifying authority has determined that the notified body does not have the capability to support existing certificates` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the provider has confirmed in writing to the national competent authorities of the Member State in which it has its registered place of business that another qualified notified body is temporarily assuming the functions` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date of the provider's confirmation` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 36(8)(b) the circumstance of point (b) holds` MEANS
        `the notifying authority has confirmed that no certificates relevant to the suspension will be issued, amended or re-issued during the course of the suspension or restriction`
    AND `the notifying authority states whether the notified body has the capability of continuing to monitor and remain responsible for existing certificates`
    AND (   (NOT `the notifying authority has determined that the notified body does not have the capability to support existing certificates`)
         OR (   `the provider has confirmed in writing to the national competent authorities of the Member State in which it has its registered place of business that another qualified notified body is temporarily assuming the functions`
             AND `the date of the provider's confirmation` AT MOST (`add months` `the date of the suspension or restriction` 3)))
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(b) the notifying authority has confirmed ... in the event that the notifying authority determines that the notified body does not have the capability ..., the provider ... shall confirm in writing ... within three months of the suspension or restriction" (a limb of a list the text introduces with "in one of the following circumstances")

-- src:614 | 8. With the exception of certificates unduly issued, and where a designation has been suspended or restricted, the certificates shall remain valid in one of the following circumstances:
@ref Art 36(8) (src:614)
-- Gloss: except for certificates that should never have been issued, when a designation is suspended or restricted the certificates stay valid in circumstance (a) or (b). The list is not closed with "only", so when neither holds the text is silent: NOTHING (fork F-36-8). A certificate unduly issued is outside the paragraph: NOTHING (fork F-36-unduly).
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the certificate was unduly issued` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the designation has been suspended or restricted` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the circumstance of point (a) holds` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the circumstance of point (b) holds` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 36(8) the certificates remain valid after a suspension or restriction` MEANS
    IF NOT (`Art 28 to 39 the notified bodies group applies on the date asked` `the date asked`)
    THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Chapter III Section 4 applies from 2 August 2025
    ELSE IF `the certificate was unduly issued`
         THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "With the exception of certificates unduly issued" (fork F-36-unduly)
         ELSE IF NOT `the designation has been suspended or restricted`
              THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "where a designation has been suspended or restricted" (a "where" condition that fails: the periods ruling of 2026-11-05, rule (b); fork F-36-where)
              ELSE IF `the circumstance of point (a) holds` OR `the circumstance of point (b) holds`
                   THEN JUST TRUE
                   ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "the certificates shall remain valid in one of the following circumstances" is not closed with "only"

§ `Article 36(9): certificates after a withdrawal`

-- src:617 | 9. With the exception of certificates unduly issued, and where a designation has been withdrawn, the certificates shall remain valid for a period of nine months under the following circumstances:
-- src:618 | (a) the national competent authority of the Member State in which the provider of the high-risk AI system covered by the certificate has its registered place of business has confirmed that there is no risk to health, safety or fundamental rights associated with the high-risk AI systems concerned; and
-- src:619 | (b) another notified body has confirmed in writing that it will assume immediate responsibility for those AI systems and completes its assessment within 12 months of the withdrawal of the designation.
@ref Art 36(9) (src:617-619)
-- Gloss: except for certificates unduly issued, when a designation is withdrawn the certificates stay valid for nine months if the competent authority has confirmed there is no risk, and another notified body has confirmed in writing that it takes immediate responsibility and completes its assessment within 12 months of the withdrawal. A certificate unduly issued is outside the paragraph: NOTHING (fork F-36-unduly).
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the certificate was unduly issued` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the designation has been withdrawn` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date of the withdrawal of the designation` IS A DATE
      `the national competent authority of the Member State in which the provider has its registered place of business has confirmed that there is no risk to health, safety or fundamental rights associated with the high-risk AI systems concerned` IS A BOOLEAN
      `another notified body has confirmed in writing that it will assume immediate responsibility for those AI systems` IS A BOOLEAN
      `that notified body completes its assessment within 12 months of the withdrawal of the designation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 36(9) first subparagraph the certificates remain valid for nine months after a withdrawal` MEANS
    IF NOT (`Art 28 to 39 the notified bodies group applies on the date asked` `the date asked`)
    THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Chapter III Section 4 applies from 2 August 2025
    ELSE IF `the certificate was unduly issued`
         THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "With the exception of certificates unduly issued" (fork F-36-unduly)
         ELSE IF NOT `the designation has been withdrawn`
              THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "where a designation has been withdrawn" (a "where" condition that fails: the periods ruling of 2026-11-05, rule (b); fork F-36-where)
              ELSE IF NOT (   `the national competent authority of the Member State in which the provider has its registered place of business has confirmed that there is no risk to health, safety or fundamental rights associated with the high-risk AI systems concerned`
                          AND `another notified body has confirmed in writing that it will assume immediate responsibility for those AI systems`
                          AND `that notified body completes its assessment within 12 months of the withdrawal of the designation`)
                   THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "under the following circumstances" (a) and (b), which the text does not close with "only"
                   ELSE IF `the date asked` LESS THAN `the date of the withdrawal of the designation`
                        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the paragraph speaks of validity after the withdrawal
                        ELSE JUST (`the date asked` AT MOST (`add months` `the date of the withdrawal of the designation` 9))  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the certificates shall remain valid for a period of nine months" (a period the text fixes: outside it, no)

-- src:620 | In the circumstances referred to in the first subparagraph, the national competent authority of the Member State in which the provider of the system covered by the certificate has its place of business may extend the provisional validity of the certificates for additional periods of three months, which shall not exceed 12 months in total.
@ref Art 36(9) (src:620)
-- Gloss: in those circumstances the national competent authority may extend the provisional validity by further periods of three months, which shall not exceed 12 months in total. Read as: the further periods add up to at most 12 months (fork F-36-9; the other reading counts 12 months from the withdrawal).
-- A "may" gated by "In the circumstances": JUST FALSE where the gate is not met, as the periods ruling's rule (b) gives (fork F-36-9, split site (ii)).
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the circumstances referred to in the first subparagraph exist` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the number of months by which the provisional validity has already been extended` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 36(9) second subparagraph the national competent authority may extend the provisional validity by a further three months` MEANS
    IF NOT (`Art 28 to 39 the notified bodies group applies on the date asked` `the date asked`)
    THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Chapter III Section 4 applies from 2 August 2025
    ELSE IF NOT `the circumstances referred to in the first subparagraph exist`
         THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "In the circumstances referred to in the first subparagraph, the national competent authority ... may extend" (a power named by "may", gated by "In the circumstances": the periods ruling's rule (b); fork F-36-9, split site (ii))
         ELSE JUST (`the number of months by which the provisional validity has already been extended` PLUS 3 AT MOST 12)  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "additional periods of three months, which shall not exceed 12 months in total" (a flat negative)

-- src:621 | The national competent authority or the notified body assuming the functions of the notified body affected by the change of designation shall immediately inform the Commission, the other Member States and the other notified bodies thereof.
@ref Art 36(9) (src:621)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the designation of a notified body has been changed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the national competent authority or the notified body assuming the functions of the notified body affected has immediately informed the Commission, the other Member States and the other notified bodies` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 36(9) third subparagraph the national competent authority or the notified body has immediately informed the Commission, the Member States and the other notified bodies` MEANS
    IF NOT (`Art 28 to 39 the notified bodies group applies on the date asked` `the date asked`)
    THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Chapter III Section 4 applies from 2 August 2025
    ELSE IF NOT `the designation of a notified body has been changed`
         THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the notified body affected by the change of designation" (fork F-unmet-where)
         ELSE JUST `the national competent authority or the notified body assuming the functions of the notified body affected has immediately informed the Commission, the other Member States and the other notified bodies`  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall immediately inform the Commission, the other Member States and the other notified bodies thereof" (a bare "shall" not done; "immediately" gives no number of days)

-- No time limit and no consequence is stated, so no trace can show this rule breached.
-- src:621 | The national competent authority or the notified body assuming the functions of the notified body affected by the change of designation shall immediately inform the Commission, the other Member States and the other notified bodies thereof.
@ref Art 36(9) (src:621)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Art 36 party` `Art 36 act`
`Art 36(9) the duty of the national competent authority to inform the Commission, the Member States and the other notified bodies` MEANS
    IF NOT (`Art 28 to 39 the notified bodies group applies on the date asked` `the date asked`)
    THEN FULFILLED  -- nothing is owed before Chapter III Section 4 applies
    ELSE PARTY `Art 36 national competent authority`
         MUST `Art 36(9) inform the Commission, the other Member States and the other notified bodies of the change of designation`
         HENCE FULFILLED

-- The provider's confirmation of point (8)(b): within three months of the suspension or restriction, where the notifying authority has determined that the notified body cannot support the certificates.
-- src:616 | (b) the notifying authority has confirmed that no certificates relevant to the suspension will be issued, amended or re-issued during the course of the suspension or restriction, and states whether the notified body has the capability of continuing to monitor and remain responsible for existing certificates issued for the period of the suspension or restriction; in the event that the notifying authority determines that the notified body does not have the capability to support existing certificates issued, the provider of the system covered by the certificate shall confirm in writing to the national competent authorities of the Member State in which it has its registered place of business, within three months of the suspension or restriction, that another qualified notified body is temporarily assuming the functions of the notified body to monitor and remain responsible for the certificates during the period of suspension or restriction.
@ref Art 36(8)(b) (src:616)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the date of the suspension or restriction` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Art 36 party` `Art 36 act`
`Art 36(8)(b) the duty of the provider to confirm in writing within three months` MEANS
    IF NOT (`Art 28 to 39 the notified bodies group applies on the date asked` `the date asked`)
    THEN FULFILLED  -- nothing is owed before Chapter III Section 4 applies
    ELSE PARTY `Art 36 provider`
         MUST `Art 36(8)(b) confirm in writing that another qualified notified body is temporarily assuming the functions`
         WITHIN (Day (`add months` `the date of the suspension or restriction` 3)) MINUS (Day `the date of the suspension or restriction`)
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST BREACH BY `Art 36 provider` BECAUSE "the provider did not confirm in writing within three months of the suspension or restriction that another qualified notified body is temporarily assuming the functions"
